Having ascended nine roles in the last few years, I recently started
playing as an archaeologist for the first time.  The first four or five
games were brutal, usually ending in less than fifteen minutes or so.  I
never found any decent weapons or armor, but just keep plugging on, and
eventually found myself deep enough that the typical denizens just
slaughtered me.

Finally, after yet another such death, I took a deep breath and decided
to straighten up and play as cautiously and slowly as necessary.  In
this new game, I found a blessed +2 elven mithril-coat just lying on the
ground on level 2.  I found a large armor shop a bit later, which my pet
helped me rob, netting me jumping boots and a cloak of invisibility.  A
bit after that, I found a bag of tricks, which I took to the nearest
altar for a sacfest.  The first sacrificable monster to emerge was a
gecko, which so impressed Quetzalcoatl that he rewarded me with
Grayswandir.  I think this is only the third time in hundreds of games
that I've had this coveted weapon in hand.

I guess I should be happy, but all I can think is "How am I supposed to
learn to handle the unique challenges of the Archaeologist role NOW?"


